{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Proofs a repository may already have, and the standard decision each one answers. The adopt script adds a ledger row for a proof only when every string under `needs` is found in the file the pointer names (for an eslint pointer, the lint configuration), every path under `files` exists, and the pointer resolves. A row added this way is claimed: the proof is named and wired in. When it is a lint rule and this plugin has texts that break the decision, adopting re-runs the rule on them and the tool holds the row from then on (checks.md).",
